import redox_driver::CheckOutcome

-- | Render a check's outcome, and decide whether it failed.
-- |
-- | Plan 50 (`docs/44 - 50 - MCP Server.md`) leaf 1 moved the check itself into
-- | `redox-driver` and left this behind. Giving the remainder a name is worth
-- | more than it looks: doc 06 §6 rule 2 — *only the CLI renders* — was a
-- | comment before this leaf, and it is now the boundary between two callers.
-- | `redox-mcp` answers the same question and must **not** have this function,
-- | because its caller wants the diagnostics as data.
-- |
-- | # Why a warning is not a failure
-- |
-- | rustc's own behaviour, and not something Redox should second-guess. Redox's
-- | lints arrive by the same route: doc 03 §12.7 makes `unwrap` *"lintable
-- | rather than prohibited"*, so a lint prints and the command carries on.
-- | [`CheckOutcome`] keeps *are there diagnostics* and *did it fail* apart for
-- | exactly this reason.
export(crate) report : &CheckOutcome -> bool -> Result<(), String>
report outcome plain =
  if .is_empty outcome.diagnostics
    return Ok ()
  rendered = redox_diag::render (&outcome.diagnostics) plain
  if outcome.failed
    return Err rendered
  eprintln! \-> "#{rendered}"
  Ok ()
